# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-6 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-6 throughout.
# H5: hand the cards back to production. This is the LAST job of the window and it runs even when a stop job (B5) halted the window
# and after a stall or a hang in FX5 or D5, which are expected to be able to leave all four cards hung with production down: the
# status of every board and the all-four reset. The driver then runs, outside this job file, the platform's fabric re-measure, the
# :latest retag in the rig daemon's local store, and placement through the admin API (which needs the user's go-ahead and an admin
# token); then /v1/models and one chat on the placed production endpoint.
# Re-place the AUDITED production image (audits on, the c2-packed-tp4 profile; tp4-serve-2 unless a later audited image passed its
# smoke and was chosen). NEVER place a gate arm: not FX5 (c2-packed-tp4-speed-fix), not D5, not any gate-only profile, and not
# tp4-serve-6 itself unless its B5 smoke passed and it was chosen. Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric
# re-measure passes, the endpoint answers /v1/models with Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt and a chat completes, and the engine log shows profile
# c2-packed-tp4 with the audits on. If the reset does not heal a board after a stall, production stays down until it does.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (it is the last job).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-6
